From 2627f91c08a2a2cb7055c11d5f982394b3a511b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mohammed Javith Akthar M <mohammedjavitham@ami.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Jun 2024 17:54:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] aspeed-video: enable partial jpeg capture support

This patch backports video driver from ASPEED SDK kernel, by
introducing partial JPEG capture functionality.

OpenBMC video driver captures entire screen region as JPEG frame. With
this enhancement, video driver can capture only the modified screen
region as smaller JPEG rectangle.

This approach can save BMC network bandwidth and CPU cycle compared to
the existing video engine configuration.

Signed-off-by: Mohammed Javith Akthar M <mohammedjavitham@ami.com>
